## MissingContentForLayout

**Severity:** error | **Type:** LiquidHtml

`{% raw %}{{ content_for_layout }}{% endraw %}` is where platformOS injects the rendered page body. A layout that never references it renders its own chrome but drops the page content entirely — a correctness defect, not a style issue.

This check runs only on layout files (`app/views/layouts/` and module layout directories); pages and partials are never flagged. Any reference to the `content_for_layout` variable clears the check, whether it is emitted with `{% raw %}{{ ... }}{% endraw %}`, `{% raw %}{% echo ... %}{% endraw %}`, or inside a `{% raw %}{% liquid %}{% endraw %}` block.

Note that named slots rendered with `{% raw %}{% yield 'name' %}{% endraw %}` are a separate mechanism and do not substitute for `{% raw %}{{ content_for_layout }}{% endraw %}`.

## Examples

### &#x2717; Incorrect Code Example (Avoid using this):

```liquid
{% raw %}
<!doctype html>
<html>
  <body>
    <header>My Site</header>
    {% yield 'footer' %}
  </body>
</html>
{% endraw %}
```

### &#x2713; Correct Code Example (Use this instead):

```liquid
{% raw %}
<!doctype html>
<html>
  <body>
    <header>My Site</header>
    {{ content_for_layout }}
    {% yield 'footer' %}
  </body>
</html>
{% endraw %}
```

## Configuration

The default configuration for this check:

```yaml
MissingContentForLayout:
  enabled: true
  severity: error
```

## Disabling This Check

This check should not be disabled — a layout without `{% raw %}{{ content_for_layout }}{% endraw %}` silently drops the page body of every page rendered with it.

## Suggestions

This check offers a suggestion (available as a quick-fix in your editor): insert `{% raw %}{{ content_for_layout }}{% endraw %}` before the closing `</body>` tag, or at the end of the layout when it has no `<body>` element.
